# The build context is everything under backend/, which includes every module's build
# directory and the Gradle caches — gigabytes of files the image has no use for, all of which
# would otherwise be sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# So: exclude everything, then name the two things the Dockerfile actually copies. Each is
# named twice, the directory and its contents, because a rule that re-includes only the
# contents leaves the directory itself excluded — the copy still works, and every build warns
# about it.
**

!app/build/install/app
!app/build/install/app/**
!migrate/build/install/migrate
!migrate/build/install/migrate/**
